    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McGovern Estates is delighted to present No. 25 Hawkins Wood Drive to the market.\r\n\r\nThis immaculately presented three-bedroom semi-detached home offers a rare opportunity to acquire a premium, A-rated family residence, ideally positioned within this highly sought-after development. The property boasts a private south-west facing rear garden, enjoying beautiful countryside views beyond, while mature amenity spaces and playgrounds are conveniently located on the doorstep.\r\n\r\nInternally, the home is tastefully decorated throughout and filled with an abundance of natural light. A particularly impressive feature is the exceptionally large attic space, offering excellent potential for future conversion, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\n\r\nTo the front, a cobblelock driveway provides generous off-street parking for two vehicles, further enhancing the practicality and appeal of this wonderful family home.\r\n\r\nMcGovern Estates highly recommends viewing No. 25 Hawkins Wood Drive to fully appreciate the quality, space and enviable setting this exceptional property has to offer.\r\n\r\nThis 3 bedroom home extends to 115m2 (1,238.93 sq.ft.) and comprises of an entrance hallway, downstairs WC, living room, kitchen/dining room, utility room, three bedrooms, one en-suite bathroom and walk-in wardrobe, a family bathroom, convertible attic space, private south/ west rear garden access. \r\n\r\nSituated in the exclusive Hawkins Wood development, No.25 is within walking distance of the thriving town of Greystones and it's marina where you can enjoy easy access to a wealth of local amenities, upscale dining, trendy boutiques, and recreational options.\r\n\r\nFor families, Greystones offers many highly regarded primary and secondary schools and a host of sports and leisure clubs abound in the area including sailing, rowing, football, rugby, tennis and GAA. \r\n\r\nThe Shoreline Leisure Centre with swimming pool and Go Gym are located close by, as are a great choice of renowned golf clubs, including Delgany, Greystones, Powerscourt and Druids Glen. \r\n\r\nJust 3km from the N11 and linked M50. Greystones is perfectly located for the commuter and served by bus and DART routes to the city centre. \r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION\r\nEntrance Hallway \r\nLaminated wood flooring, alarm panel, carpeted stairs to landing, recess lighting, cloakroom and WC off hallway.\r\n\r\nDownstairs WC\r\nTiled floor with part tiled walls, WC, wash hand basin, chrome heated towel rail, recess lighting, extractor fan, exterior window.\r\n\r\nLiving Room \r\nLaminated wood flooring, overlooking front driveway.\r\n\r\nKitchen/ Dining Room\r\nTiled flooring, fully fitted kitchen, floor and wall based storage cupboards, stainless steel sink unit, countertops with breakfast bar, extractor fan, double doors leading to south west facing rear garden.\r\n \r\nUtility Room\r\nTiled floor, plumbed for washing machine and dryer, significant storage space, smoke alarm, extractor fan.\r\n\r\nLanding\r\nCarpeted stairs and landing, hot press off landing, attic access via Stira stairs, smoke alarm.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \r\nCarpeted floor, floor to ceiling built-in wardrobes ,walk in wardrobe, smoke alarm. \r\n\r\nEn Suite\r\nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin, fully tiled shower cubical with mains power shower, chrome heated towel rail, extractor fan, external window.\r\n \r\nBedroom 2\r\nCarpeted flooring, floor to ceiling built-in wardrobe, smoke alarm, picture window overlooking south west facing rear garden.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\nCarpeted flooring, smoke alarm, picture window overlooking south west facing rear garden.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom \r\nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin, fully tiled bath with mains power shower, extractor fan, external window.\r\n\r\nOutside Rear Garden\r\nPrivate beautifully landscaped south/west facing rear garden with paved patio, power point, side access gate.\r\n\r\nOutside Front Garden\r\nCobblelock driveway with off-street parking for two cars, mature plants and hedges.\r\n\r\nSPECIAL FEATURES\r\nA2 rated family home \r\nPrivate cul de sac location\r\nOff street parking for 2 cars\r\nAmple visitor parking\r\nImmaculately presented \r\nLarge attic space with potential to convert\r\nPrivate south/ west facing rear garden \r\nAir to Water heating system\r\nDouble glazing throughout\r\nOwner occupied \r\nFully alarmed\r\nBroadband available\r\nMature amenity greens\r\nCharlesland shopping complex a short walk away\r\nShoreline gym and swimming pool nearby\r\nClose to Greystones Town & Marina\r\nN11/M50 road network easily accessible\r\nBus and DART transport near by\r\n\r\n*Management fees 528.27 -Per annum including bins"
      },
